// FUNCTION: BFME2 0x0025EC22 size=218 name=?getScreenCornerWorldPointsAtZ@View@@UAEXPAVCoord3D@@000M@Z evidence=X:retail PE exports class Coord3D: ??0Matrix4D@@QAE@ABVCoord3D@@@Z tier=B hypothesis:cohesion
// The view's size and origin bound the screen; the four corners are unprojected at z.
void View::getScreenCornerWorldPointsAtZ(Coord3D *topLeft, Coord3D *topRight, Coord3D *bottomLeft, Coord3D *bottomRight, Real z)
{
	ICoord2D screenTopLeft, screenTopRight, screenBottomLeft, screenBottomRight;
	ICoord2D origin;
	Int viewWidth = getWidth();
	Int viewHeight = getHeight();

	if (topLeft == 0 || topRight == 0 || bottomLeft == 0 || bottomRight == 0)
		return;

	getOrigin(&origin.x, &origin.y);
	screenTopLeft.x = origin.x;
	screenTopLeft.y = origin.y;
	// The width's value is numbered after origin.x, so the shared sum is built width-first
	// (lea edx,[edi+eax]) as in retail; the conditional is a no-op for the compiler's numbering.
	screenTopRight.x = origin.x + (viewWidth ? viewWidth : viewWidth);
	screenTopRight.y = origin.y;
	screenBottomLeft.x = screenTopRight.x;
	screenBottomLeft.y = origin.y + viewHeight;
	screenBottomRight.x = origin.x;
	screenBottomRight.y = origin.y + viewHeight;

	screenToWorldAtZ(&screenTopLeft, topLeft, z);
	screenToWorldAtZ(&screenTopRight, topRight, z);
	screenToWorldAtZ(&screenBottomLeft, bottomLeft, z);
	screenToWorldAtZ(&screenBottomRight, bottomRight, z);
}

